# =============================================================================
#  Optional frontend settings
# =============================================================================
#  You almost certainly do not need this file. It documents the one escape
#  hatch in api.js, so that the reason it exists is written down somewhere.
#
#  Copy to .env.local only if you actually need the override.
# =============================================================================

# Where the API lives.
#
# LEAVE IT UNSET. Unset means every call is a relative /api/... URL against
# whatever host is serving the page, which is the arrangement the whole design
# wants, and all the normal setups produce it:
#
#   development   src/setupProxy.js forwards /api to Spring Boot on 8443
#   production    the rewrite in vercel.json forwards /api to the backend
#
# Same-origin is what lets both cookies stay first-party and SameSite=Lax, which
# is CSRF protection you get for free and never have to maintain.
#
# Setting this points the frontend straight at the backend's own hostname, which
# makes the page and the API different sites. If you do that you must ALSO set,
# on the backend:
#
#   APP_CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://your-app.vercel.app
#   APP_COOKIE_SAME_SITE=None
#   APP_COOKIE_SECURE=true
#
# ...and you have then given up the Lax protection and taken on third-party
# cookie blocking as a live risk. See DEPLOYMENT.md.
#
# REACT_APP_API_BASE=https://your-service-yourorg.koyeb.app
